Note = {Emerging Technology for Sustainable Development Congress (ETSDC), Univ
   Kebangsaan Malaysia, Fac Engn \& Built Environm, Bangi, MALAYSIA, AUG
   05, 2014},
Abstract = {High temperature and humidity oblige occupants to use mechanical
   ventilation to regulate indoor temperature in tropical climate.
   Therefore, energy consumption becomes a challenge facing the designers
   in primary steps of design. Natural ventilation known as a passive
   design strategy in buildings is one of the innovative techniques in
   modern building to reduce operation costs and energy consumption.
   Although the advantages of natural ventilation are proved by previous
   studies, few studies have been done on application of openings and
   apertures designs to maximize indoor air velocity inside the buildings.
   This study reviews different ventilation methods and techniques which
   have been applied through openings to identify the most effective
   architectural elements for adequate ventilation inside the buildings.
   Comparison of study results shows that building orientation accompanying
   with apertures size are effective design strategies and techniques to
   increase indoor air ratio. Finally, the study recommends various form of
   openings and different form of louvered windows as research gaps for
   further study.},
