Year = {2008},
Pages = {578-582},
Note = {International Conference on Informational Technology and Environmental
   System Science, Henan Polytechn Univ, Jiaozuo, PEOPLES R CHINA, MAY
   15-17, 2008},
Abstract = {Realizing sustainability is the problem needs to be solved urgently. It
   is essential to select an appropriate method to assess sustainable
   development. This paper takes Heilongjiang province as the research
   object to analyze sustainable development by ecological footprint from
   1995 to 2005. The arable land contributed most to the ecological
   footprint among the six components of the ecological footprint per
   capita of Heilongjiang Province. It is consistent with the actual
   situation. The total ecological footprint has risen from 8.19x10(7) gha
   in 1995 to 9.44x10(7) gha in 1997, and then declined little to 8.79 x
   10(7) gha in 1998, whereafter increases to 1.24x10(8) gha in 2005. The
   total ecological capacity tends to increase from 8.66x10(7) gha in 1995
   to 9.25x10(7) gha in 2005. Although the ecological capacity increased a
   little, it is slower then the ecological footprint rising. The results
   show that Heilongjiang province is suffered unsustainable during the
   year 1996, 1997, 2004 and 2005. The main reason is exploiting and
   consuming natural resource in excess and the improper economy increasing
   manner.},
