Organization = {Xinjiang Univ; Hebei United Univ},
Abstract = {A rapid quantitative risk evaluation system of non-point source
   pollution (NPSP), based on comprehensive consideration of various
   factors such as topographic features, land use construction, annual mean
   precipitation, soil erosion characteristics and pollutant removal cost,
   was constructed using an Spatial Analysis Module of GIS on watershed
   scale. We investigated the risk pattern of NPSP in the Dianchi Lake
   Watershed using the rapid risk assessment system. The results indicated
   that NPSP risk pattern showed the arc or normal distribution trend in
   the Dianchi Lake Basin, namely the medium risk area of NPSP is the
   largest (about 1311 km(2)). Moreover, the spatial difference of high
   risk NPSP pattern is remarkable: the high risk region for NPSP was
   primarily in the 10 km range of the southern and eastern parts and the 5
   km range of western part around the Dianchi Lake.},
