Abstract = {Pot experiment on red soil (garden soil) contaminated by heavy metal was
   conducted in Guixi, Jiangxi, China. The five treatments included the
   control (CK), application of lime at 1.20 (LimeLow) and 2.4 g.kg-1
   (LimeHigh), organic fertilizer (hollow swine feces) at 6.0 g kg-1
   (OMlow) and 12.0g.kg-1(OMHigh) were conducted. The results indicate that
   using lime to tune soil pH to light alkalescence could improve net
   photosynthesis significantly, increase soil microbe C (especially for
   cellulose-decomposing bacterium), reduce the available content of heavy
   metal for the growth of plants, and serves as a viable treatment of soil
