Organization = {Singapore Inst Elect (SIE)},
Abstract = {Cleaning strategies for algae-fouled ultrafiltration membrane were
   investigated in pilot-scale experiments. Comparison of five different
   physical cleaning modes indicated that backwashing followed by forward
   flushing was more effective for flux recovery, and combining hydraulic
   cleaning with air sparge could improve the permeate flux recovery
   percent up to 87.49\%. Cleaning frequency should be taken for the
   concentration of foulants and cleaning methods. To maximize flux
   recovery for the algae-fouled membrane, on-line chemical cleaning was
   studied, the permeate flux reduced only 5.37\% after over 240h
   filtration duration. (C) 2011 Published by Elsevier Ltd. Selection
