   Sci \& Arts; Georgian Acad Sci; Acad Fine Arts \& Design Bratislava;
   Russian Acad Arts; Turkish Acad Sci; SGEM},
Abstract = {State of reproductive health of the population is the major aspect of
   the social and demographic development of the country which in many
   respects defines also the development level of the society as a whole.
   Without reliable and qualitative information about reproductive
   population health, first of all women, without knowledge about their
   relation to the health, the birth of children, to family values, their
   estimate of maternity obstetric service it is impossible to pursue
   successful demographic policy.
   In 2011 Rosstat together with Ministry of Health of Russia, in
   partnership with UN Fund in the field of population and the Center for
   control and prevention of diseases (USA) for the first time in our
   country conducted examination of reproductive health of women.
   Examination was conducted in 60 subjects of the Russian Federation where
   more than ten thousand women were interrogated {[}1].
   The Federal State Statistics Service provided an access to inspection
   microdata on the basis of which we conducted research of key aspects of
   reproductive health of the population in Russia.
   The main emphasis in research was placed on the analysis of the
   following groups of indicators:
   Birth rate and child mortality.
   Planning of a family and reproductive perceptions.
   Risky behavior concerning health (smoking and alcohol consumption).
   Health and behavior of youth.
   HIV/AIDS and other STD.
   On the basis of the received results recommendations for public agencies
   of Russia on development of the programs directed on improvement of the
   demographic situation and reproductive health of women were prepared.},
