Pages = {121-126},
Note = {1st Conference School and Health 21, Brno, CZECH REPUBLIC, SEP 15-16,
   2005},
Abstract = {The paper has been carried out on the psychosomatic and psychosocial
   negative effects of hypokinesis on the people health. Practising sport
   produces changes on a physical level that can bring about changes in the
   psyche or in interpersonal relations, e.g., relief of unnecessary
   physical tension and social adaptation, and also changes in
   self-concept. The project ``Health 21{''} brings new aims - teacher like
   an important part of prevention and creation of a new subject ``Health
   Education{''} in schools. The project is planned in such a way that the
   intervention program works with its specific means (activities, methods
   and techniques choice) through one pet-son (teacher, coach) sympathising
   with the other person who has some specific problems and needs help
   (pupils, young sportsmen). There is the new prepared study program of
   ``Health Education{''} presented as well as the results of two research
   projects with analysis of alcohol consumption and smoking of 400 young
   athletes (13-18 years old), and the problem of the obesity and the
   positive yoga intervention by children in elementary school. In this
   case the experimental sample included 24 children from 400 tested
   persons - from 400 persons 120 had overweight. The use of yoga
   techniques, physical, breathing and relaxation exercises seems to be
   effective in the therapy of obesity children, mainly for positive
   changes in motor skills, weight reduction and also in their
   self-perception and self-efficacy. This changed self-image is the result
   of cognitive, emotional and social variables that the children absorb
   during the program.},
