Abstract = {In this paper, we propose a method of measuring free flow speed
   according to different water depth in the ponding situation. With
   different water depth, changes of tire-road friction coefficient caused
   by reduction of the wheel load are different. This coefficient brings
   great effect to vehicle's free flow speed. In order to reveal this
   phenomena, observations data obtained in the year 2009 at the number 202
   state road in Japan, which runs through Fukuoka, Itosima. By measuring
   the recording data, we got the speed range corresponding to different
   water depth. The purpose of this study is to obtain variation of free
   flow speed according to different water depth and lay foundations for
   numerical modeling in the future.},
