Note = {International Conference on Social Sciences and Education (ICSSE),
   Bandung, INDONESIA, NOV 21-23, 2017},
Abstract = {Substance refers to any Drugs, Medication or toxins that share the
   potential of abuse. The usage of substances harmful to human health is
   known to be the substance abuse. Adolescence is the crucial period in
   the life span of a person where many starts using substances like
   tobacco alcohol and illicit drugs in their daily life. It is clear that
   there is a need to understand these problems among adolescents. Usages
   of substances are a leading cause of death and debilitating state among
   adolescents. This study aims to assess the perception of adolescents
   with regard to substance abuse, to understand the myths related to
   substance abuse and the need to develop Social Work Training Module.
   This was a cross-sectional study conducted on college students (n = 80)
   aged 17-20 years. Descriptive survey design was used. The data was
   collected in the colleges of Mangalore. Knowledge of students on
   substance abuse and Myths was determined by administering structured
   questionnaire. From the study findings, it is revealed that majority of
   the students (53.75\%) had Good knowledge regarding substance abuse and
   its ill effects. The mean percentage of knowledge score was 42.27\%
   (mean: 21.56 +/- 4.20). Majority of the students (47.50\%) agreed Myths
   as Facts, which highlights the need for educational module which in turn
   will help in reduction of this menace among Adolescents. Present study
   highlights the need for spreading more awareness about Substance abuse,
   its myths, and associated problems. The study has conceptualized a
   module consisting of 7 sessions of duration which will be done and
   tested by the authors.},
